    {
      "ancestors": [],
      "attributes": [
        {
          "doc_text": " Returns a rather crude approximation (upper bound) for the maximum buffer size",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19663,
            19745
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " calculated from the given decoded exponent.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19746,
            19793
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19794,
            19797
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " The exact limit is:",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19798,
            19821
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19822,
            19825
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " - when `exp < 0`, the maximum length is `ceil(log_10 (5^-exp * (2^64 - 1)))`.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19826,
            19907
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " - when `exp >= 0`, the maximum length is `ceil(log_10 (2^exp * (2^64 - 1)))`.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19908,
            19989
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19990,
            19993
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " `ceil(log_10 (x^exp * (2^64 - 1)))` is less than `ceil(log_10 (2^64 - 1)) +",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19994,
            20073
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " ceil(exp * log_10 x)`, which is in turn less than `20 + (1 + exp * log_10 x)`.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            20074,
            20156
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " We use the facts that `log_10 2 < 5/16` and `log_10 5 < 12/16`, which is",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            20157,
            20233
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " enough for our purposes.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            20234,
            20262
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            20263,
            20266
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Why do we need this? `format_exact` functions will fill the entire buffer",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            20267,
            20344
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " unless limited by the last digit restriction, but it is possible that",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            20345,
            20418
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " the number of digits requested is ridiculously large (say, 30,000 digits).",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            20419,
            20497
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " The vast majority of buffer will be filled with zeroes, so we don't want to",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            20498,
            20577
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " allocate all the buffer beforehand. Consequently, for any given arguments,",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            20578,
            20656
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " 826 bytes of buffer should be sufficient for `f64`. Compare this with",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            20657,
            20730
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " the actual number for the worst case: 770 bytes (when `exp = -1074`).",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            20731,
            20804
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        }
      ],
      "body_range": [
        20848,
        20921
      ],
      "kind": "fn",
      "name": "estimate_max_buf_len",
      "range": [
        19663,
        20921
      ],
      "signature_range": [
        20805,
        20847
      ]
    },
    {
      "ancestors": [],
      "attributes": [
        {
          "doc_text": " Formats given floating point number into the exponential form with",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            20923,
            20993
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " exactly given number of significant digits. The result is stored to",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            20994,
            21065
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " the supplied parts array while utilizing given byte buffer as a scratch.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            21066,
            21142
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " `upper` is used to determine the case of the exponent prefix (`e` or `E`).",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            21143,
            21221
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " The first part to be rendered is always a `Part::Sign` (which can be",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            21222,
            21294
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " an empty string if no sign is rendered).",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            21295,
            21339
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            21340,
            21343
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " `format_exact` should be the underlying digit-generation function.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            21344,
            21414
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " It should return the part of the buffer that it initialized.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            21415,
            21479
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " You probably would want `strategy::grisu::format_exact` for this.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            21480,
            21549
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            21550,
            21553
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " The byte buffer should be at least `ndigits` bytes long unless `ndigits` is",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            21554,
            21633
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " so large that only the fixed number of digits will be ever written.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            21634,
            21705
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " (The tipping point for `f64` is about 800, so 1000 bytes should be enough.)",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            21706,
            21785
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " There should be at least 6 parts available, due to the worst case like",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            21786,
            21860
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " `[+][1][.][2345][e][-][6]`.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            21861,
            21892
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        }
      ],
      "body_range": [
        22219,
